# SQLAlchemy Models and Migrations

- Field names are `snake_case` and match the database column names.
- `metadata` is reserved by SQLAlchemy. Use a trailing underscore with an explicit column name:
  `metadata_ = Column("metadata", JSONB, ...)`.
- Be explicit about relationship cascades (for example `cascade="all, delete-orphan"`).
- All schema changes go through Alembic migrations; never alter schema in runtime code.
- Keep structural integrity in DB constraints (unique, check, foreign key). Enforce complex domain
  rules in services and validators.
- Add indexes deliberately for lookup and default-resolution paths.
- Instance time-series data storage is under design; see `docs/plans/instance-data-storage.md`
  before adding columns or tables for it.

```python
# ❌ BAD
metadata = Column(JSONB)

# ✅ GOOD
metadata_ = Column("metadata", JSONB, nullable=False, server_default=text("'{}'::jsonb"))
```

Full reference: `docs/conventions/framework-conventions.md`.
